          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong pre-abelian category
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              (an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
              with finite
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproducts
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
          %p Equivalently:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong pre-abelian category
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
              with all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              and finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p These two definitions are indeed equivalent.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the discussion
              %a{:href => "finite+limit#Properties"} here
              the existence of finite limits is equivalent to that of finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of two morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              in an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              is the same as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo −
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f-g
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              in a pre-abelian category, the operations of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorders"} preorders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(c)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"}> subobjects
              ) into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Quot
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quot(c)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
              out of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %p
              In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:b\to c
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = ker(coker(f))
              and dually.
          #DecompositionOfMorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              in a pre-abelian category has a canonical decomposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} coker
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A\stackrel{p}\to \coker(\ker f)\stackrel{\bar{f}}\to\ker(\coker f)\stackrel{i}\to B
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monic
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              in the above decomposition is always an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Of course every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                is pre-abelian.
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion-free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
                in all of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ab
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2:\mathbb{Z}\to \mathbb{Z}
                is not a kernel.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p
            The concept “pre-abelian category” is part of a sequence of concepts of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+and+abelian+categories"} additive and abelian categories
